Hey, everyone several things to keep in mind:

# Delivery launch doesn’t assume any one-time operations costs; 
## Delivery itself costs to rider = Bolt tariff + 20 UAH, 20% = 4UAH we earn, out of which 1 UAH goes to insurance. We have not changed ASP in the budget as 15000 deliveries would not change ASP for 1,3 mln rides.
# We insure deliveries with the help of our current partner - 1UAH per each delivery, which is giving us 0.038 EUR per delivery, max delivery we expect per month is 15,000 => 15,000*0,038 EUR = 570 EUR, rouded to 600 eur.
# Line 71 of the budget includes insurance cost but there is no interdependence link in the budget between number of rides/deliveries, as it’s forecasted as an average for three previous months.

# We are updating the budgets this week for Dec19 and Q12020, so we will manage to add 600 eur/monthly on top of other opex.  I will personally confirm here as far as we finalize the final numbers with the team.
# We do not expect that Delivery will be a significant part of our  business in UA, but we target the following goals:
- increase utilisation and average drivers EPH; 

      - respond to one of the most frequent b2b requests, which use it as documents delivery  service;  

     - have competitive range of services offered on the market (local competitors, including Uklon, have it);

Is it enough for getting greenlight for delivery re-launch?

